# evidence-for: US-005, FR-014, FR-036, FR-040, AC-019, AC-020, AC-021, AC-043
#
# US-005. Four trees. A tree of well-formed stubs is not checked and says so
# with a count rather than claiming every page matched its declared type. The
# same tree with one stub that never said who it is for exits 1 instead: a
# frontmatter defect on a stub is a real finding and beats not-checked. The
# grep after it counts the prose findings on those same placeholder braces --
# which name `create_item`, `/dashboard` and `--verbose` -- and the count is
# zero, because a skeleton is not writing.
#
# The last two runs are one tree in two states, and they are why the pass line
# is worded the way it is (D-094). Mixed, the run reads one page, exits 0, and
# says so over the pages it read, with the stub count beside it: a stub is
# counted among the pages in the header line, declares a doc_type of its own,
# and is never matched against it. With the marker deleted from that same stub
# and no other byte touched, the three tokens inside its braces are reported.
# The sentence "every page matches its declared type" was printed over the
# first of those two runs.

